            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_2",
            "review_title": "Review at Velo Book Cafe",
            "review_text": "Teaveex3\n27 contributions\n0\nJust a bad experience for me\nAug 2016 • Solo\nThis cafe is located two doors down from Moon Cafe right off the Dragon Bridge.\nIt has a cute book exchange/book decoration atmosphere, but downstairs was pretty hot even with a fan rotating on me.\n\nPrice is average for a coffee shop.\n\nCoffee was average and the fries came in a smaller portion than I'm used to, but the worst part about my experience was right when I arrived.\n\nI pull into the sidewalk and park my scooter as an employee hands me my ticket(valet I guess?) for the scooter...I'm walking to my table and I hear a scooter hit the ground. I turn around and two female employees are struggling to pick my boyfriend's scooter back up. If this was America I would freak out and demand their information in order to get payment for the damages, but as I'm not accustomed to their culture and what to do in this situation, I simply watched them and let them know I saw exactly what just happened. Maybe they would initiate some sort of apology or money for the damages....Nope. \n\nThey proceeded to move the scooter across the street. I sat, got my coffee and read a bit before leaving due to the heat(and slight hunger). I walk across the street to get on the scooter and as I pull the brake I feel something on my fingers. I pick my hand up off the brake...paint chips all over my hands and coming off the brake. So frustrated, I drive home and promise to never come back to this cafe.\n\nGranted it was a mistake by two employees and pretty much has nothing to do with the quality/atmosphere/price of the cafe, but due to this experience during my first visit I will not ever return, nor will my boyfriend.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten September 4, 2016",
