            "review_title": "Review at Velo Book Cafe",
            "review_text": "YJ\nSingapore, Singapore47 contributions\n0\nNice cafe with lots of manga!!\nDec 2015 • Couples\nThis cafe is quite cute for the following reasons:\n1) It is three stories high, super big (also, conveniently located beside the dragon bridge)\n2) When we went on a weekday, it was super duper packed, and 80% of the patrons were students, busy studying, each of them bought a drink or two \n3) They have very little food options on their menu, but we did get their French fries and instant noodles (which I thought it was nice that they put so many ingredients in it and made it so presentable and also it was yummy -- see photo uploaded)\n4) They provide free manga books for their customers to read, but the books are in Vietnamese\n5) If you sit on the second or third floors, you have to take off your shoes and place them on the shoe rack provided on the first floor\nI guess this place targets students, providing them a venue to study. But we spent a lovely 3-4 hours there relaxing.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 24, 2015",
